 "why": "In the 14 days from 7 February 2021, ERCOT North Hub real-time price averaged USD 3,047.37 per MWh against USD 21.46 per MWh in the 14 days before, a rise of USD 3,025.91 per MWh. The control, NYISO New York City real-time price, went from USD 56.85 per MWh to USD 66.35 per MWh, a rise of USD 9.51 per MWh. The difference between the two changes is USD 3,016.40 per MWh, standard error USD 1,598.93 per MWh (Newey-West, 3 lags, 28 days). That difference is within 1.96 standard errors of zero: no difference beyond the error. This is the difference between two changes over these days and its error; it does not say what produced it.",
